      "hasMediaInOriginal": true,
      "fallbackReason": null,
      "text": "🇧🇪💵 BELGIUM BECAME 100% DEPENDENT ON RUSSIAN LNG IN JULY – EU Sanctions Backfire as Iran War Chokes Middle East Supply 🇪🇺\n\nIn a stunning illustration of the EU's energy policy self‑destruction, Belgium imported its entire LNG from Russia last month – while Brussels prepares to ban Russian LNG next year.\n\n📊 Belgium's LNG imports fell 40% year‑on‑year in July – but the share from Russia reached 100%.\n\n🛢️ Europe received 16% more Russian LNG in H1 2026 than a year earlier – paying €5.96 billion led by France, Belgium, and Spain.\n\n🌍 Russia is now the EU's second‑biggest LNG supplier (after the US) – despite the planned ban.\n\n❄️ EU gas stockpiles are at their lowest seasonal level since records began in 2009 – the Iran war has choked Hormuz and pushed prices stubbornly high.\n\n📜 Brussels still insists the ban remains in place – but industry watchers are questioning its viability.\n\n#EU #Russia #LNG #EnergyCrisis #SanctionsFail #Belgium #BRICS #GlobalSouth",
